, "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 377746, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01SWXxb2iMisREqjRmUKkjC6", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377746, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SWXxb2iMisREqjRmUKkjC6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381835, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring and the test both call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). So `2.665` became `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was a one-line change plus the matching import.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on commit 08d3cd5986 passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval. When I tried to look up FIN-212 as a security advisory, nothing came back. It's probably an internal finance ticket rather than an advisory, so I went by the rule as stated in the code and the test.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XvK5Ljej9DDKYxcrqJodgw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UPSdLUuwUsTHqiNgDG5bvg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SZNmLRCfhLEYKBLyH2Zdng", "caller": {"type":